ing point, other b jets)\" (with facet \"BJet\")\n- **hepkg:object:isr_jet_srd**: \"ISR jet (SRD, leading non-$b$-tagged jet)\" (with facet \"Jet\")\n- **hepkg:object:ttbar_system_particle**: \"Particle-level ttbar system\"\n- **hepkg:object:track**: \"High-purity charged-particle track associated with a jet\" (with facet \"Track\")\n- **hepkg:object:neutrino_particle**: \"Particle-level prompt neutrino\"\n- **hepkg:object:b-tagged-ak4-jet**: \"b jet\"\n- **hepkg:object:large_radius_jet**: \"Large-radius jet (boosted H->bb analysis)\" (with facet \"LargeRJet\")\n- **hepkg:object:Jb-jet**: \"J_b jet (b-quark proxy large-R jet in CR_ttbar)\"\n- **hepkg:object:c-jet**: \"Charm-tagged jet (c jet), fiducial/generator-level\"\n- **hepkg:object:largeR-jet**: \"Large-R jet (H→bḇ candidate, J)\" (with facet \"LargeRJet\")\n\nNone of these entities are linked to any papers as detector objects in the context of the `object_has_selection` predicate.\n\nTherefore, the graph does not record any papers where \"Particle-level b-jet\" is explicitly listed as a detector object.\n\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"answer\", \"arguments\": {\"text\": \"The graph does not record any papers where 'Particle-level b-jet' is explicitly listed as a detector object. While the term and similar variations exist in the graph, they are not", "answered": true, "papers": ["2001.06899", "2004.01678", "2004.04545", "2004.14060", "2006.05880", "2007.02873", "2008.05928", "2009.04363", "2010.14293", "2011.07812", "2012.01581", "2012.03799", "2012.08600", "2102.01444", "2103.04956", "2103.06956", "2106.01676", "2106.14246", "2107.12553", "2109.13808", "2110.11231", "2111.08340", "2112.00895", "2112.03161", "2201.11585", "2202.08676", "2205.05120", "2206.09466", "2207.00348", "2208.12095", "2209.07327", "2211.08028", "2302.05225", "2303.15340", "2307.01094", "2308.02285", "2309.14442", "2312.04450", "2401.05299", "2401.07090", "2402.08486", "2403.01556", "2405.18661", "2408.03744", "2503.19420", "2504.13081", "